        "Naaman is a commander of Aram, Israel’s military enemy, yet the narrator says the LORD had given Aram victory through him. That claim unsettles narrow assumptions about where God may act. Naaman also has tsara‘at, a broad biblical category for serious skin conditions; it should not automatically be identified with modern Hansen’s disease. The unnamed Israelite girl was taken captive in a raid. Her witness is honored, but her enslavement is neither approved nor repaired in the story.",
